### Exercise 4 — Status flows
#
# Run these with the VS Code REST Client extension (humao.rest-client, already recommended
# for this project): click "Send Request" above any request below. No shell needed — works
# the same on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
#
# The response pane shows the HTTP status line (e.g. `HTTP/1.1 204 No Content`) at the top.
#
# These requests CHAIN: send them top to bottom. Later requests reuse the travel ID from the
# first response automatically (REST Client "request variables"), so nothing is hardcoded —
# it adapts to whatever sample data this run generated.
#
# `cds watch` must be running with Exercise 4's basic Open -> Accepted flow.
# Run this before the optional InReview extension. Once acceptTravel requires InReview,
# use ex5.http to submit for review and ex9.http to check acceptance instead.
# The lookup needs an Open travel. If it returns an empty value array, use the lookup and
# valid-create requests in ex3.http to create one, then send this file top to bottom.

@host = http://localhost:4004
@auth = alice:

### 1) Find an Open travel (status_code `O`) — SEND THIS FIRST
# @name openTravel
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels?$select=ID,description,status_code&$filter=status_code eq 'O'&$top=1
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 2) Accept that travel — expect HTTP 204, status flips to Accepted
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{openTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})/TravelService.acceptTravel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 3) Confirm the status flipped automatically (expect "status_code":"A")
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{openTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})?$select=description,status_code
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}

### 4) Illegal transition — accept the same travel again (no longer Open), expect HTTP 409
# CAP rejects it: code "INVALID_FLOW_TRANSITION_SINGLE".
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{openTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})/TravelService.acceptTravel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 5) Reopen the travel — expect HTTP 204, back to Open
POST {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{openTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})/TravelService.reopenTravel
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### 6) Confirm the status is Open again (expect "status_code":"O")
GET {{host}}/odata/v4/travel/Travels({{openTravel.response.body.$.value[0].ID}})?$select=description,status_code
Authorization: Basic {{auth}}
